HOW TO IDENTIFY WHICH TYPE — DECISION GUIDE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Read the problem. Ask these questions in order:

Is it a BST and are you using left < root < right to navigate?
→ YES → Type 5 (BST)

Does it ask for level-by-level processing, minimum depth,
or right/left side view?
→ YES → Type 2 (BFS Level Order)

Does it involve a path (root-to-leaf or any-node-to-any-node)?
→ YES → Type 4 (Path Problems)
Does the path start at root? → pass remaining sum down.
Can it start anywhere? → postorder + global max.

Does it ask for a tree-wide property (depth, diameter, balance)?
→ YES → Type 3 (Tree Properties)
Ask: "what do I need from each child to compute this at the node?"

Otherwise (visit nodes in a specific order, collect values)?
→ YES → Type 1 (DFS Traversal)
Need sorted order from BST → inorder.
Build/serialize tree → preorder.
Compute subtree values → postorder.

